description:
Use this tool to create a WhatsApp message template.

For this tool's 'template_json' property, pass a JSON matching this shape:

{
  "name": string,
  "language": string,
  "category": "MARKETING" | "AUTHENTICATION" | "UTILITY",
  "components": Component[],
}

General rules:
- name must be lowercase snake_case.
- category must be uppercase.
- language must be a WhatsApp locale code such as "en_US", "tr", "es", "pt_BR".
- Only include fields supported by the component variant.
- Do not include null fields.
- Components should normally be ordered as:
  1. header, if any
  2. body
  3. footer, if any
  4. buttons, if any
- A template can have at most one header, one body, one footer, and one buttons component.
- BODY is required unless the user is clearly creating a special authentication template handled elsewhere.
- HEADER and FOOTER are optional.
- BUTTONS are optional.

Component variants:

1. Text header without variables

{
  "type": "HEADER",
  "format": "text",
  "text": "Your order update"
}

Use this when the header is plain text.

2. Text header with variables

{
  "type": "HEADER",
  "format": "TEXT",
  "text": "Hi {{1}}",
  "example": {
    "header_text": ["Alice"]
  }
}

Rules:
- Text header supports template variables.
- If text contains variables, include example.header_text.
- The example array must contain sample values in the same order as the variables appear.
- For named parameters, the placeholder names appear in text, but the examples are still values.

3. Image header

{
  "type": "HEADER",
  "format": "IMAGE",
  "example": {
    "header_handle": ["https://example.com/sample-image.jpg"]
  }
}

Use this when the template header should contain an image.
The example should be a sample image handle or URL when available.

4. Video header

{
  "type": "HEADER",
  "format": "VIDEO",
  "example": {
    "header_handle": ["https://example.com/sample-video.mp4"]
  }
}

Use this when the template header should contain a video.
The example should be a sample video handle or URL when available.

5. Document header

{
  "type": "HEADER",
  "format": "DOCUMENT",
  "example": {
    "header_handle": ["https://example.com/sample-document.pdf"]
  }
}

Use this when the template header should contain a document.
The example should be a sample document handle or URL when available.

6. Location header

{
  "type": "HEADER",
  "format": "LOCATION"
}

Use this when the template should display a location/map header.

Important:
- For template creation, LOCATION is only the header format.
- Do not put latitude, longitude, address, or name in the template creation component.
- The actual location values are supplied later when sending the approved template, not when creating the template.

7. Body without variables

{
  "type": "BODY",
  "text": "Your order has shipped and is on the way."
}

Use this for the main message text.

8. Body with variables

{
  "type": "BODY",
  "text": "Hi {{1}}, your order {{2}} has shipped.",
  "example": {
    "body_text": [
      ["Alice", "ORD-12345"]
    ]
  }
}

Rules:
- If body text contains variables, include example.body_text.
- body_text is an array containing one array of sample values.
- The inner array values must match the variables in order of appearance.
- Use placeholders like {{1}}, {{2}}.

9. Footer

{
  "type": "FOOTER",
  "text": "Reply STOP to unsubscribe."
}

Rules:
- Footer is plain text only.
- Do not use variables in footer text.

10. Buttons wrapper

{
  "type": "BUTTONS",
  "buttons": [
    Button
  ]
}

Rules:
- Buttons must be inside a single component whose type is "BUTTONS".
- Do not place button objects directly in components.
- Button text should be short and action-oriented.

Button variants:

A. Quick reply button

{
  "type": "QUICK_REPLY",
  "text": "Confirm"
}

Use when the user should tap a predefined reply.

B. Phone number button

{
  "type": "PHONE_NUMBER",
  "text": "Call us",
  "phone_number": "+15551234567"
}

Use when the user should call a business phone number.
phone_number must include country code.

C. Static URL button

{
  "type": "URL",
  "text": "View order",
  "url": "https://example.com/orders"
}

Use when the button always opens the same URL.

D. Dynamic URL button

{
  "type": "URL",
  "text": "View order",
  "url": "https://example.com/orders/{{1}}",
  "example": ["ORD-12345"]
}

Rules:
- Use this when the final URL path or query contains a variable.
- The example array contains the sample value for the dynamic URL part.

E. Copy code button

{
  "type": "COPY_CODE",
  "example": "SAVE20"
}

Use for coupon or promo-code templates.
The button copies the provided code when the template is sent.

G. OTP button

{
  "type": "OTP",
  "otp_type": "COPY_CODE",
  "text": "Copy code"
}

For one-tap OTP:

{
  "type": "OTP",
  "otp_type": "ONE_TAP",
  "text": "Copy code",
  "autofill_text": "Autofill",
  "package_name": "com.example.app",
  "signature_hash": "abc123"
}

Rules:
- Use OTP buttons only for authentication templates - category should be "AUTHENTICATION". Authentication templates can only be created for WABAs that have a 2,000 messaging limit or above.
- Do not use marketing or utility wording in authentication templates.

Examples:

Utility order update with named parameters:

{
  "name": "order_shipped_update",
  "language": "en_US",
  "category": "UTILITY",
  "components": [
    {
      "type": "HEADER",
      "format": "TEXT",
      "text": "Order {{1}} update",
      "example": {
        "header_text": [["ORD-12345"]]
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "BODY",
      "text": "Hi {{1}}, your order has shipped and should arrive by {{2}}.",
      "example": {
        "body_text": [
          ["Alice", "Friday"]
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "FOOTER",
      "text": "Thank you for shopping with us."
    },
    {
      "type": "BUTTONS",
      "buttons": [
        {
          "type": "URL",
          "text": "Track order",
          "url": "https://example.com/orders/{{1}}",
          "example": ["ORD-12345"]
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}

Utility store location template:

{
  "name": "store_location_info",
  "language": "en_US",
  "category": "UTILITY",
  "components": [
    {
      "type": "HEADER",
      "format": "location"
    },
    {
      "type": "BODY",
      "text": "Hi {{1}}, here is the location of our {{2}} store.",
      "example": {
        "body_text": [
          ["Alice", "Downtown"]
        ]
      }
    }
  ]
}
